# Call-site ledger of sqlparse 0.6.1 (sqlparse/, commit 09dbe1eec31ed1b3cd05366748865f11ba427d32).
# Hand-written from the source and Python semantics; judgements and statistics in sqlparse.md.
#
# Value sets used below (sqlparse.md, "Value dispatch"):
#   preprocess filters: KeywordCaseFilter (_CaseFilter.process), IdentifierCaseFilter, TruncateStringFilter.
#   stmtprocess filters: StripTrailingSemicolonFilter, SpacesAroundOperatorsFilter, StripCommentsFilter,
#     StripWhitespaceFilter, ReindentFilter, AlignedIndentFilter, RightMarginFilter.
#   postprocess filters: SerializerUnicode, OutputPythonFilter and OutputPHPFilter (OutputFilter.process).
#   _group callbacks: the local match, valid(_prev/_next/_final) and post functions of the group_* functions.
#   Token types: _TokenType.__getattr__ runs on the first load of a child type only (sqlparse.md, token types).
default reject sqlparse.tokens._TokenType.__getattr__: Python calls __getattr__ only when the normal lookup fails on a _TokenType instance. At this site the receiver is not a token type (a module, a class, a token or token list, a filter, a Lexer, a StatementSplitter, a FilterStack, a DelimitedSpans, a super() object, a file or sys stream, a str, bytes, a list, a dict, a re.Match, an argparse object, or another object that is not a token type), or it is a token type whose attribute already exists: the first load of a child type stores it in the parent's instance dict (setattr, tokens.py:26), and the module code that `import sqlparse` runs (tokens.py, sql.py, engine/grouping.py, keywords.py) creates every token type that the package names, except Comment.Multiline and Comment.Multiline.Hint. The sites that create a token type accept the candidate explicitly
default reject sqlparse.sql.TokenList.__getitem__: no TokenList is subscripted, iterated, unpacked, searched with `in` or converted here; the operand is a list (self.tokens, a slice of it, the filter lists, the lists of grouping and filters), a tuple, a str, a dict, a re.Match, a generator or other iterator, an argparse value, a typing construct in an annotation, or a client object; the sites that subscript or iterate a TokenList accept it explicitly
default reject sqlparse.sql.TokenList.__iter__: no TokenList is iterated, unpacked, searched with `in` or converted here; the operand is a list (self.tokens, a slice of it, the filter lists, the lists of grouping and filters), a tuple, a str, a dict, a generator or other iterator, an argparse value, or a client object; the sites that iterate a TokenList accept it explicitly
default reject sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_typecasts.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_tzcasts.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_typed_literal.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_period.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_as.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_assignment.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_comparison.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_arrays.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_operator.match, sqlparse.engine.grouping.group_identifier_list.match: a local function of its group_* function, which passes it to _group; only _group calls it, through its parameter `match` (grouping.py:532). A call `x.match(...)` is the method Token.match of a token

